{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSbX2mfrbLfAxYcNmd2C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand the codebase structure. Let me summarize my analysis findings:\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a POST `/orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that manages order status transitions, cancels associated shipments in CREATED state, and ensures idempotent cancellation with transactional integrity.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order.kt:11-16 — Order entity currently lacks status field\n- OrderController.kt:15-46 — Handles POST /orders (creates) and GET /orders/{orderId} (reads)\n- Shipment.kt:9-27 — Shipment entity has status (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED) already defined\n- ShipmentController.kt:26-44 — Creates shipments but doesn't validate order status\n- ApiExceptions.kt:11-30 — Exception hierarchy with ConflictException (409), ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- ApiError.kt:31-37 — ErrorCode enum needs expansion\n- GlobalExceptionHandler.kt — Centralized exception-to-HTTP conversion\n\n**Conventions in this repository:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiExceptions (not return error responses); GlobalExceptionHandler converts them\n2. ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409\n3. ErrorCode enum for machine-readable error codes\n4. ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(...) for POST endpoints\n5. Tests use MockMvc with @BeforeEach clearing repositories\n6. Tests verify both status code AND error envelope JSON shape (e.g., `$.error.code`)\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt — Add OrderStatus enum and status field\n2. OrderController.kt — Initialize order status to ACTIVE; add cancel endpoint\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt — Add findByOrderId(orderId) method\n4. ShipmentController.kt — Before creating shipment, check order exists and isn't CANCELLED\n5. ApiError.kt — Add ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n6. OrderControllerTest.kt — Add 5 cancel scenarios\n7. ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Add test for shipment creation on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotency: cancelling already-CANCELLED order must succeed silently\n- Atomicity: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, cancel fails and nothing changes\n- Shipment lifecycle: only CREATED shipments can be cancelled, not CONFIRMED or CANCELLED ones\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket is explicit about all cases.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status: OrderStatus field. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add @PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\") that:\n   - Finds the order (throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found)\n   - If already CANCELLED, return it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException and change nothing\n   - Otherwise, set order to CANCELLED, cancel all CREATED shipments, save order, return it\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `fun findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to query shipments by order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — In the create endpoint, after checking duplicate shipmentId, check that the order isn't CANCELLED. If it is, throw ConflictException. If order doesn't exist, proceed as before (don't error — this is the \"keep its current behaviour\" requirement).\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Add ORDER_CANCELLED error code to ErrorCode enum.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add 5 tests:\n   - Cancel ACTIVE order → returns CANCELLED order, shipments CREATED → CANCELLED\n   - Cancel already CANCELLED order → succeeds, returns CANCELLED order\n   - Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment → 409 ConflictException, nothing changes\n   - Cancel nonexistent order → 404 ResourceNotFoundException\n   - Create shipment for CANCELLED order → 409 ConflictException\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add 1 test:\n   - Create shipment for CANCELLED order → 409 ConflictException\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- *Creating a service layer*: The controllers currently interact directly with repositories. Adding a service would be out-of-scope refactoring. Keeping logic in the controller keeps the change minimal and consistent with existing style.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Cancel ACTIVE order with CREATED shipments:*\n1. POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n2. OrderController finds O-1 (ACTIVE)\n3. Queries ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(O-1) → [S-1 (CREATED), S-2 (CREATED)]\n4. No CONFIRMED shipments, so:\n   - Set order status to CANCELLED\n   - Update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Save order\n   - Return order with status=CANCELLED\n5. Response: 200 OK, Order(status=CANCELLED)\n\n*Cancel already CANCELLED order:*\n1. POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n2. OrderController finds O-1 (CANCELLED)\n3. Return 200 OK with same order (no change)\n\n*Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment:*\n1. POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n2. OrderController finds O-1 (ACTIVE)\n3. Queries ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(O-1) → [S-1 (CONFIRMED)]\n4. CONFIRMED shipment found → throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED, message)\n5. Response: 409 Conflict, error envelope with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n6. Database state unchanged\n\n*Create shipment for CANCELLED order:*\n1. POST /shipments with orderId=O-1 (CANCELLED)\n2. ShipmentController checks if shipment already exists (no)\n3. Checks if order exists and isn't CANCELLED → order is CANCELLED\n4. Throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED, message)\n5. Response: 409 Conflict\n\n*Create shipment for nonexistent order:* — No check (proceed as before; this keeps the test behavior unchanged)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nTests will be added to OrderControllerTest (5 scenarios) and ShipmentControllerTest (1 scenario):\n\n1. `cancel_active_order_returns_cancelled_and_cancels_created_shipments` — Creates order O-1 and shipments S-1 (CREATED) and S-2 (CREATED), cancels order, verifies order is CANCELLED and both shipments are CANCELLED.\n\n2. `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_idempotently` — Creates order, cancels it, cancels again, verifies no error and order still CANCELLED.\n\n3. `cancel_with_confirmed_shipment_returns_409_and_changes_nothing` — Creates order O-1 and shipment S-1 (CONFIRMED), attempts cancel, verifies 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code, verifies order still ACTIVE and shipment still CONFIRMED.\n\n4. `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404` — Attempts to cancel nonexistent order, verifies 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code.\n\n5. `cancel_returns_the_order_with_status` — Creates order and cancels, verifies response body contains status field set to CANCELLED.\n\n6. `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409` (in ShipmentControllerTest) — Creates order O-1, cancels it, attempts to create shipment, verifies 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code.\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3311,"cache_read_input_tokens":21441,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3311},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"645daa5c-a17d-42a8-894a-c1c453f11995","uuid":"440f0965-300d-4bde-8adc-ab27361ad37c","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:23:23.280Z","request_id":"req_011CfSbX2KtEe8YJwuARRYDH"}
