{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSbgVRoJGcsS2xhs3YzN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` completed successfully with all 22 tests passing (13 original + 9 new)\n\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 4 original OrderControllerTest tests, 5 original ShipmentControllerTest tests, 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests, and 3 CustomerControllerTest still pass\n\n3. ✅ **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's CREATED shipments** — Implemented in OrderController.cancel() with test `cancel_ACTIVE_order_with_CREATED_shipments_cancels_the_shipments`\n\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Uses ConflictException for 409, ResourceNotFoundException for 404, same error envelope pattern as existing endpoints\n\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** — Covered by tests:\n   - `cancel_already_CANCELLED_order_succeeds_idempotently` — idempotent success\n   - `cancel_with_CONFIRMED_shipment_returns_409_and_changes_nothing` — all-or-nothing on conflict\n   - `cancel_returns_404_for_nonexistent_order` — unknown order handling\n   - `rejects_shipment_creation_for_cancelled_order_with_error_envelope` — shipment validation\n\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — No changes to pom.xml\n\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified order, shipment, and api feature files; only touched test files for those same features\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- **Order.kt** — Added OrderStatus enum and status field with ACTIVE default; change was necessary to track order state\n- **OrderController.kt** — Added cancel endpoint with ShipmentRepository dependency; necessary for the core feature\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added findByOrderId() method; necessary to query shipments for cancellation check\n- **ShipmentController.kt** — Added order existence and cancellation check; necessary per requirement \"Creating a shipment for a cancelled order is rejected with HTTP 409\"\n- **ApiError.kt** — Added ORDER_CANCELLED error code; necessary for the new error scenario\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 7 tests covering all cancel scenarios; necessary to verify the new endpoint works correctly\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 2 tests for shipment creation on cancelled order and non-existent order; necessary to verify the new validation\n\nAll changes are minimal and directly related to the ticket requirements.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are satisfied, all tests pass, and the error handling follows existing patterns.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that manages order status (ACTIVE/CANCELLED), cancels CREATED shipments, ensures idempotent cancellation with transactional consistency, and prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       Order.kt — Added OrderStatus enum and status field to track order lifecycle\n              OrderController.kt — Added cancel endpoint with transactional consistency check for CONFIRMED shipments\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — Added findByOrderId() to query shipments by order for cancellation\n              ShipmentController.kt — Added validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n              ApiError.kt — Added ORDER_CANCELLED error code for new error scenarios\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — Added 7 tests for cancel endpoint scenarios\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Added 2 tests for shipment validation with cancelled orders\n\nTests         cancel_ACTIVE_order_returns_CANCELLED_order — verifies status transition\n              cancel_ACTIVE_order_with_CREATED_shipments_cancels_the_sh